{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788287730,"nonce":"uyaTPYbMfeKVYJr17weFTaEL2Fk=","title":"No verb can set a temperature target, so a built freezer can only hold the vanilla 21C default","message":"Found by the M2 rehearsal (session 18), one step past the room that met M2.\n\n## What happened\n\n`templates/freezer-kitchen.ir.json` was placed, built by colonists, and wired to\nthe power room's generator. `digest.power` went from `draw_w: 0` to `draw_w: 40`\nwhen the trunk closed, so the two coolers are on the net and running. The freezer\nhalf then sat at **14.6 C against a 16 C outdoors** — cooling by about a degree\nand a half, which is not a freezer.\n\nNothing is broken. A `Cooler` carries `CompTempControl` with a default\n`targetTemperature` of 21 C, so with the room already at 14.6 the comp is at its\nlow-power idle — which is exactly what a 40 W draw across two coolers means\n(2 x ~175 W x 10%). The building works. **The agent has no way to tell it what\ntemperature to hold.**\n\n## The gap\n\n    grep -rl \"CompTempControl\\|targetTemperature\\|TargetTemperature\" Source/AutoRimmer/\n    -\u003e no matches\n\nNothing in the mod touches temperature control at all. There is no verb to read a\ncooler's or heater's target, and none to set it. `flick` toggles power and is the\nnearest thing, which is the wrong knob: switching a cooler off is not the same as\ntelling it to hold -10 C.\n\n## Why it matters more than one missing setter\n\n`templates/INDEX.md` lists `freezer-kitchen`'s carried lessons as \"**cold that is\nchecked**, clean that is measured, haul paths short, 400 W that has to come from\nsomewhere\". Three of those four are reachable today — `room` publishes `temp_c`\nand `Cleanliness`, `digest.power` publishes the draw. **\"Cold that is checked\" is\nnot**, because the template can only ever hold the vanilla default, and 21 C is\nnot cold. A template whose stated lesson no verb can exercise is a template that\ncannot be graded, which makes this a 4.1/4.4 problem as much as a verb gap.\n\nIt also blocks the obvious M1 follow-on: food preservation is the reason a colony\nbuilds a freezer, and `digest.resources.food_days` cannot be affected by a\nbuilding the agent cannot configure.\n\n## Where the gate lives\n\n`RimWorld/CompTempControl` holds `targetTemperature` and the def-side\n`TemperatureControlProps` carry `minTemperature` / `maxTemperature`, which is the\nrange the UI slider is clamped to — so the widget's gate is that clamp plus the\ncomp's presence, not a new invention. `Building_Cooler` / `Building_Heater` are\nthe `TickRare` consumers. The verb should re-implement that clamp and cite it,\nper DESIGN's Action model, rather than writing the field raw.\n\nWorth checking while implementing, not assumed here: whether reading the comp is\nfree of the lazy-getter hazard `WorldSafe` catalogues, and whether the vent\n(`Building_Vent`) belongs in the same verb or is a `flick` case.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A verb reads, for every temperature-controlled building on the map or in a\n  named room: def, position, current target, the def's min/max clamp, whether it\n  is powered, and the room it serves. Reading mutates nothing.\n- Setting a target below the def's `minTemperature` is a REFUSAL naming the\n  clamp and the value, not a silent clamp-and-succeed — the project's standing\n  rule that a wrong argument is loud.\n- On the session-18 fixture: set the two `freezer-kitchen` coolers to a freezing\n  target, advance, and `room --id \u003cfreezer\u003e` reports a temperature below zero\n  while `digest.power.draw_w` rises off its idle floor. That is \"cold that is\n  checked\" becoming reachable, and it is the criterion that matters.\n- A cooler with no power refuses or reports `powered: false` rather than\n  accepting a target that cannot be honoured.\n- Journaled like any other player verb, with the before/after target.\n\nCross-refs: `54b0c9a`, `36999fd` and the `fc287ba` comment are the other three\nfindings from the same run; `accept/runs/s18-20260901/` has the fixture this\nissue's acceptance refers to.","files":null}]}